{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-74084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =4+0+0-4 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-4)+(-1)\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-8-1+0+3 \\\\  & =-6.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =0-3+6-3 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is $v$ and $x$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74084" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ce03934dd8681099f3b791de03dd62be1d5945c02fb1f7e22fbb089bb563b8e"} {"question" "q-74084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$v$ and $w$ only"] ["text" "$v$ and $x$ only"] ["text" "$v$ only"] ["text" "$w$ and $x$ only"] ["text" "$x$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74084" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$v$ and $x$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74089" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74089" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 0+5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-4-1+0+5 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2-4-3+5 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4+0-6-5 \\\\  & =-7.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is $v$ and $w$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74089" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ce03934dd8681099f3b791de03dd62be1d5945c02fb1f7e22fbb089bb563b8e"} {"question" "q-74089" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74089" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$v$ and $w$ only"] ["text" "$v$ and $x$ only"] ["text" "$v$ only"] ["text" "$w$ only"] ["text" "$x$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74089" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$v$ and $w$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =0-4-6+10 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0-2+0+2 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =0-1-9-4 \\\\  & =-14.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is $v$ and $w$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ce03934dd8681099f3b791de03dd62be1d5945c02fb1f7e22fbb089bb563b8e"} {"question" "q-74077" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74077" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$v$ and $w$ only"] ["text" "$v$ and $x$ only"] ["text" "$w$  only"] ["text" "$x$  only"] ["text" "$x$ and $w$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-74077" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$v$ and $w$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2+3-4-3 \\\\  & =-2.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 5+(-1)\\cdot 0+4\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5-8+3 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 3+3\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =1+2+12-15 \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is $w$ and $x$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ce03934dd8681099f3b791de03dd62be1d5945c02fb1f7e22fbb089bb563b8e"} {"question" "q-39914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$v$  only"] ["text" "$v$ and $w$ only"] ["text" "$v$ and $x$ only"] ["text" "$w$ and $x$ only"] ["text" "All of the listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$w$ and $x$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vector $u=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $u?$\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We compute the dot product between $u$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot (-7)+8\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =5-7+16-15 \\\\  & =-1.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {w}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {w}_{4} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot (-5)+8\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =15-5-8-6 \\\\  & =-4.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot x & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {x}_{4} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-1)+8\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5-1+8-12 \\\\  & =-10.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct option is 'None of the listed'." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39993" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ce03934dd8681099f3b791de03dd62be1d5945c02fb1f7e22fbb089bb563b8e"} {"question" "q-39993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$v$ and $w$ only"] ["text" "$v$ only"] ["text" "$w$  only"] ["text" "$x$ only"] ["text" "None of the listed"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39993" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "None of the listed"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -k\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ k \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that  $u⊥v.$ Find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =k\\cdot k+(-5)\\cdot k+(-1)\\cdot 3+(-k)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-5k-3+3k \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-2k-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-2k-3 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+1) & =0 \\\\ k & =-1,3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/state.json" "file_sha256" "56f304f8890eaa4f2636f91cbc3f677f46d197552a57c2617b406e4f0a9e1b4c"} {"question" "q-39988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044739/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ce03934dd8681099f3b791de03dd62be1d5945c02fb1f7e22fbb089bb563b8e"} {"question" "q-39988" "field" "selection" "attribute" "ans